      "body": "Done in 71d20af and ea39db2.\r\n\r\nNow if you select multiple tokens and add a tag, the tokens will be grouped.\r\n\r\n![screen shot 2018-10-12 at 07 34 54](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1454404/46850143-f9b57a80-cdf2-11e8-8ca7-5adca02ad57c.png) ... becomes ... ![screen shot 2018-10-12 at 07 35 12](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1454404/46850145-fae6a780-cdf2-11e8-95a5-8a7734c736fe.png)\r\n\r\nNote that tokens are grouped even if they are not consecutive, so if I select \"Alice\" and \"Alice's\" and then set a tag, then this will happen:\r\n\r\n![screen shot 2018-10-12 at 07 47 54](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1454404/46850185-29fd1900-cdf3-11e8-8c06-48daec6aec3e.png)\r\n\r\nThis is probably not useful, but it is the easiest way to do this. If it is a requirement, we can also check for consecutive-ness.",
